      "feedback": "Yes. **This one has more genuinely interesting material than the Fiji Fan Palm, but I would make you rewrite it before I'd be comfortable seeing it on a serious botanical-garden QR page.** There are several places where the prose is excellent, several where you're mixing fact with inference, and a few where I think the underlying botany needs correction.\n\nIf I were the Selby/palm person who scanned this, my reaction would be:\n\n> **“Oh, this is interesting. Xate, Maya use, the floral trade, the bamboo resemblance, the invasive issue—there's a real story here. But why am I reading a NASA houseplant study and a herbarium bombing story before you've told me the most important thing about this palm?”**\n\nThe good news is that I think **this could become one of your better pages.**\n\n---\n\n# First: what is the actual story of this palm?\n\nI'd rank the stories like this:\n\n### 🔥 The big stories\n\n**1. This is a Central American forest-understory palm that has been used by people for centuries.**\n\n*",
